 "fieldData": {
  "awb---how-to-step-3-des": "Under whatever leads the page, add two or three plain links: the homepage, your most visited section and a way to contact you.",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"404 Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a 404 page?\", \"a\": \"A 404 page is what a website shows when someone requests a URL that does not exist on it, sent along with the HTTP 404 status code. The page itself can be anything the site designs, from one line of plain text to a full layout with links back in.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a 404 page for my website?\", \"a\": \"Check your host's documentation for its error page setting. On GitHub Pages, a file named 404.html in the root of the publishing source becomes the site's 404 page. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe the page, and the prompt can ask for unknown URLs to return a 404 status.\"}, {\"q\": \"What causes 404 page not found?\", \"a\": \"The requested address points nowhere on the server. Someone mistyped it, the page was deleted, or it moved without a redirect while old links kept the old address.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I access a 404 page?\", \"a\": \"Most people reach one by accident, and getting past it takes a minute. Check the address for a typo, shorten the URL to its parent folder, or search the site for the page title.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you give me some examples of 404 error pages?\", \"a\": \"Galleries such as 404s.design and Awwwards collect 404 page examples you can browse by style. When you study them, look past the illustration at what each page offers next. The same rule applies to a thank you page: the next step matters more than the art.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to find a website 404 page?\", \"a\": \"Add a made-up path to the domain, such as example.com/no-such-page, and whatever loads is that site's 404 page. Repeat it under a section such as /blog/ or /docs/ to see whether that part of the site has its own version.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some funny 404 error pages?\", \"a\": \"Funny 404 pages work when the joke is one line and the way out is obvious, like a coffee roaster's \\\"We spilled this page\\\" above a link to the shop. Skip the humor on sites people need for critical services. US federal design guidance advises against whimsical error messages there, since a visitor may not appreciate the joke.\"}, {\"q\": \"Why use a custom 404 page?\", \"a\": \"To keep a visitor who followed a dead link on your site. A custom 404 page can carry your menu and a search box, where a generic error screen leaves the back button as the only way out.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do the best 404 pages have in common?\", \"a\": \"Short copy and a clear way back in. The best 404 pages name the problem in a line, then offer a search box or a link to the section people visit most. Under the design, they still return a real 404 status code, which keeps the dead URL out of Google's index.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do 404 pages hurt SEO?\", \"a\": \"No. A 404 on a URL that should not exist is normal, and Google has said these errors do not hurt how the rest of a site ranks. So 404 error page SEO comes down to the pages that should exist, and pages built to rank deserve the same care as any landing page seo work.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
